    {
      "id": "4yjqhew",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Matter"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Matter is anything that possesses mass, occupies space, and can be perceived by our senses.",
        "The five fundamental states of matter are Solid, Liquid, Gas, Plasma, and Bose-Einstein Condensate (BEC).",
        "Density represents the mass per unit volume of a substance and determines whether an object floats or sinks.",
        "Changes in state (melting, freezing, vaporization, condensation, sublimation) occur due to temperature and pressure variations.",
        "Elasticity is the property by which a material regains its original shape and size after the removal of deforming forces.",
        "Pressure is defined as the force applied perpendicular to the surface of an object per unit area."
      ],
      "id": "ni9132y"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lzp1qdq",
      "content": "• Matter is anything that has mass and occupies space."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bl2a0o4",
      "content": "• It is made up of tiny particles called atoms and molecules."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0gminuf",
      "content": "• Matter exists in different forms in nature."
    },
    {
      "id": "36ufq8h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. States of Matter"
    },
    {
