          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lvpjfem",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Physical Properties of Matter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9bb1zwt",
      "content": "• Mass – amount of matter in a substance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u37qdil",
      "content": "• Volume – space occupied by matter."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Matter and Its Properties",
      "id": "oi379zy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bm10lix",
      "content": "• Density – mass per unit volume."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n5jq8ye",
      "content": "• Elasticity – ability of a material to regain its original shape."
    },
    {
      "id": "eo00bej",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Changes in States of Matter"
    },
    {
      "id": "pq1oxa6",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Process</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Melting</p>",
            "<p>Solid changes into liquid</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Freezing</p>",
            "<p>Liquid changes into solid</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Evaporation</p>",
            "<p>Liquid changes into gas</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Condensation</p>",
            "<p>Gas changes into liquid</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sublimation</p>",
            "<p>Solid changes directly into gas</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ay0d91g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Density"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1nj60az",
      "content": "Density is defined as mass per unit volume."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Property",
        "Solid",
        "Liquid",
        "Gas"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Shape & Volume",
          "Fixed shape and volume",
          "Indefinite shape, fixed volume",
          "Indefinite shape and volume"
        ],
        [
          "Intermolecular Force",
          "Very strong",
          "Moderate",
          "Extremely weak"
        ],
        [
          "Compressibility",
          "Negligible",
          "Low",
          "Very high"
        ],
        [
          "Fluidity",
          "Cannot flow",
          "Flows from higher to lower level",
          "Flows in all directions"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "yxt7rml"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pk21nvz",
      "content": "Formula: Density = Mass / Volume"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "24qewhi",
      "content": "SI Unit of Density = kg/m³"
    },
    {
      "id": "ub1qwgr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Elasticity"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eiuzfhk",
      "content": "Elasticity is the property of a material to regain its original shape after deformation when the external force is removed."
    },
    {
      "id": "azs8xfs",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Pressure"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3axq3nx",
      "content": "Pressure is defined as force acting per unit area."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ey0k2lv",
      "content": "Formula: Pressure = Force / Area"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "6hw5r4e",
      "content": "SI Unit = Pascal (Pa)"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Plasma is the 4th state of matter consisting of super energetic, ionized gas particles, responsible for the glowing in stars and sun.",
        "Hooke's Law states that within the elastic limit, stress is directly proportional to strain (Stress / Strain = Constant).",
        "Atmospheric pressure decreases with altitude, which causes the boiling point of water to decrease at higher elevations."
      ],
      "id": "zmxm18f"
    },
    {
